, business, computer science, journalism, social work, teacher education, a dual BS/MS degree in Occupational Therapy, and one of the top-ranked nursing programs in New York State, provide students with opportunities to study liberal arts, sciences, and professional programs. The College also offers six graduate programs: Aviation Management, Clinical Trials Management, Pharmaceutical Science and Business, Physician Assistant, Social Work and Nursing Education. Located in Queens, the most ethnically diverse county in New York State, the College enrolls 7,000 students from over 95 nations. Nine out of ten students are members of a racial/ethnic minority group, and more than half of undergraduates are the first in their families to pursue higher education. The College’s 50-acre campus encompasses seven buildings, including science and computer labs, music and television studios, a Performing Arts Center, and a Health and Physical Education Center. The College recently completed seven major construction projects, with more scheduled for the future. In addition, its neighborhood is at the center of a renaissance fueled by economic revitalization. York College is committed to fostering integrity, diversity, intellectual discovery, and civic engagement to benefit its students, the community, and the world. The Department of Business and Economics at York College/CUNY invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Information Systems and Business anticipated to begin Fall 2027. York College is located in Queens, one of the five boroughs of New York City and one of the most ethnically diverse counties in the nation. It is a senior college within The City University of New York and is situated on a 50-acre campus in the heart of the Downtown Jamaica section of the borough. The Department of Business and Economics seeks a dynamic scholar and educator with expertise in Information Systems and the ability to contribute broadly to the Department’s undergraduate business curriculum. The successful candidate will teach courses in Information Systems and related technology-focused business disciplines, as well as contribute to other business and economics offerings based on departmental needs. Teaching assignments may include courses in Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Cybersecurity, AI, Business Analytics, Digital Transformation, Enterprise Systems, Business Technology, and other subject areas in the department such as International Business, Management, Operations Management depending on the candidate’s expertise and departmental requirements. Teaching assignments may include day, evening, and weekend courses. The successful candidate will: Demonstrate effectiveness in teaching Information Systems and other assigned courses. Develop and deliver courses that integrate current technologies, industry practices, analytical approaches, and emerging trends in business. Contribute to curriculum development, assessment, and continuous improvement initiatives within the Department. Mentor and advise students pursuing careers in business, information systems, analytics, cybersecurity, AI, and related fields. Support experiential learning opportunities, including internships, applied projects, industry partnerships, and student organizations. Engage in scholarly research and professional activities consistent with the expectations of a tenure-track faculty appointment. Contribute to department, college, and university service activities. Collaborate with colleagues across business disciplines to enhance program quality and relevance. Maintain relationships with business organizations, professional associations, industry partners, and community stakeholders. Perform other responsibilities assigned by the Department Chair. QUALIFICATIONS The successful candidate must possess: A PhD or other relevant doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, Business Analytics, or a closely related discipline by the time of appointment (Fall 2027). Demonstrated ability to teach effectively in Information Systems and/or related disciplines. Ability to teach undergraduate courses in Information Systems and contribute to additional courses aligned with departmental needs. Evidence of scholarly potential through research, publications, conference presentations, working papers, or other scholarly activities. Commitment to student success through effective teaching, advising, mentoring, and support of diverse student populations. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders. Preferred Requirements Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate: Expertise in Information Systems, including areas such as: Business analytics. Artificial intelligence Digital transformation. Database systems. Systems analysis and design. Cybersecurity. Enterprise systems. Cloud computing. Information technology management. Ability to teach courses across multiple business disciplines, including one or more of the following: Entrepreneurship and innovation. International Business. Management. Marketing. Operations Management. Business Strategy. Economics. Quantitative methods for business. A strong research agenda with potential for continued scholarly contributions. Experience incorporating technology, analytics, applied projects, case studies, and experiential learning into instruction. Experience supporting students from diverse backgrounds and preparing them for careers in business and technology. Professional experience or industry engagement relevant to Information Systems or business disciplines. Experience developing or revising curriculum to address changing workforce and industry needs. Evidence of professional recognition through publications, grants, industry partnerships, leadership roles, or service contributions. COMPENSATION $82,384 - $98,231 - Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs.  We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. HOW TO APPLY Candidates for faculty positions should provide (i) a cover letter explaining interest in, and qualifications for, the position; (ii) curriculum vitae/resume, (iii) evidence of teaching excellence, (iv) a statement of teaching philosophy, (v) a research statement, and (vi) the names, titles, and contact information (telephone and email) for three professional references. Please submit your application online through this job board as follows: •    Go to www.cuny.edu and click on Employment Select \"Apply Now\" then create or login to a user account and provide the requested information. •    Click on Job Postings on CUNYfirst •    Click Search job listings •    Click on More search options •    Search by Job Opening ID number 32739 *In order to be considered for this position, applicants must include a cover letter, CV/Resume, and contact information (email and telephone) for three references. Please upload these as ONE document in rtf, doc, or pdf format. CLOSING DATE October 11, 2026 (Job posting will be removed at 12am) JOB SEARCH CATEGORY CUNY Job Posting: Faculty EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply.  At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups.  Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32739 Location: York College Apply Now For information on requesting a reasonable accommodation in the application process, visit the Company career page. INFORMATION FOR Future Students Current Students Faculty & Staff FINANCIAL AID Applying for Financial Aid Pell/TAP Need-Based Support Scholarships and Grants Estimating College Costs RESOURCES CUNYfirst | Blackboard Combating Sexual Misconduct (Title IX) Freedom of Information Law (FOIL) CUNY Builds: CUCF Procurement Emergency Preparedness QUICKLINKS Find People (phone/emails) University Advancement Communications and Marketing Media Relations CUNY Arts CUNYMatters Employment Sell to CUNY Copyright 2026 Privacy Security Accessibility Terms of Use CUNY Alert Contact Us facebook twitter youtube linkedin Flickr We use cookies to improve your experience on our site. To find out more, read our privacy policy . Accept Cookies Decline Cookies"
